# Local-only secrets for `wrangler dev`. Copy this file to `.dev.vars`
# (already gitignored) and fill in real values. For staging/production, use
# `wrangler secret put <NAME> --env <env>` instead — never commit a real
# secret to this repo, and never add one as a plaintext `wrangler.toml` var.

# Optional. Unset by default on every environment, including production.
# When set, a request to POST /v1/qr carrying a matching
# `X-Dynamic-QR-Test-Override` header is granted the dynamicQr entitlement
# regardless of the deployed environment's default — see
# src/lib/entitlements.ts for the fail-closed rules this follows (an unset
# value here means the override path does not exist at all, not "matches
# everything"). Intended use: testing Dynamic QR end-to-end against a
# `production`-configured backend without enabling the feature for real
# production traffic. Generate a real value with, e.g.:
#   node -e "console.log(crypto.randomUUID())"
# DYNAMIC_QR_TEST_OVERRIDE_SECRET=
